== the numbered list prints every entry ==
    1  echo one
    2  ls
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== a trailing count prints only the most recent entries ==
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== a non-numeric count is rejected without printing the list ==
1:9: error: Builtin `history`: 'foo' is not a valid count.
     1 |  history foo; echo "rc=$?"
       |          ^~~
rc=2
== a count past the list size still prints every entry, no overflow ==
    1  echo one
    2  ls
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== the print flag echoes its operands and stores nothing ==
alpha
beta
== builtin history -a no longer reports an unknown builtin ==
continued
== type reports the builtin ==
history is a shell builtin
== clear empties the list ==
cleared
== history -r reads a named file into the list ==
    1  existing one
    2  existing two
    3  merged alpha
    4  merged beta
== history -r on a missing file errors ==
rc=1
== history -r rejects invalid data without changing the list ==
rc=1
    1  existing one
    2  existing two
    3  merged alpha
    4  merged beta
== history -r separates an unterminated backing record ==
    1  tail
    2  next
== an empty import creates a missing backing file ==
rc=0
== history accepts high bytes as file data ==
rc=0
1
== an oversized decoded record is omitted ==
0
== concurrent history stores preserve both records ==
2
== running shells reload history written by another instance ==
    1  shared-event
== KOSH_HISTORY_SIZE controls the visible retained window ==
    4  four
    5  five
    1  one
    2  two
    3  three
    4  four
    5  five
== a stored multiline event keeps its submitted shape ==
    1  line one
line two
